From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 08:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ui/dbus: do not abort the machine on a scanout with no texture

dbus_scanout_texture() asserts on tex_id, so a zero one takes down the
whole VM:

  qemu-system-x86_64: Failed to call update: The connection is closed
  qemu-system-x86_64: Failed to call update: The connection is closed
  Assertion failed: tex_id (ui/dbus-listener.c: dbus_scanout_texture: 450)

Observed with a Windows guest on virtio-vga-gl whose display powered off
after an idle timeout, against a D-Bus display client that had gone away
earlier - the listener is only unregistered from dispose, so it keeps
being called after its peer disconnects, and the first scanout without a
texture is fatal.

A missing texture is a frame we cannot show, not a state the machine
cannot continue from. Report it and skip the frame.

The listener outliving its connection is a separate problem and is left
alone here.

Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/tools/qemu-xen/ui/dbus-listener.c b/tools/qemu-xen/ui/dbus-listener.c
index a54123a..23467fd 100644
--- a/tools/qemu-xen/ui/dbus-listener.c
+++ b/tools/qemu-xen/ui/dbus-listener.c
@@ -447,7 +447,17 @@ static void dbus_scanout_texture(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
     uint32_t stride, fourcc;
     uint64_t modifier;
 
-    assert(tex_id);
+    if (!tex_id) {
+        /*
+         * virgl has no texture for this scanout: the guest freed the
+         * resource (a display powered off after an idle timeout does it),
+         * or the GL context went away with a listener whose peer has
+         * already disconnected. Neither is a reason to abort a running
+         * machine - skip the frame and keep the guest alive.
+         */
+        error_report("%s: no texture for scanout, skipping", __func__);
+        return;
+    }
     fd = egl_get_fd_for_texture(tex_id, (EGLint *)&stride, (EGLint *)&fourcc,
                                 &modifier);
     if (fd < 0) {
